    <!-- 06 The Andromeda Effect -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="andromeda">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Andromeda</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The Andromeda effect: why fatigue accelerated in 2024&ndash;2026</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Meta&rsquo;s Andromeda ad-ranking system (2024) changed the game</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Creative lifespan compressed from ~6 weeks average to ~10 days</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The system aggressively penalizes stale creative and rewards freshness</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In 2024, Meta rolled out Andromeda &mdash; a new ad-ranking system that fundamentally changed how ads are evaluated and delivered. Andromeda processes far more ad candidates per impression (up from ~1,000 to ~100,000+) and weights <strong>creative freshness</strong> as a significant ranking signal. The result: ads that would have run profitably for 4&ndash;6 weeks in 2023 now decay in 10&ndash;14 days.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What Andromeda changed</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Faster audience saturation.</strong> Andromeda finds the optimal audience faster, which means it also exhausts that audience faster. Peak performance arrives sooner, but so does fatigue.</li>
          <li><strong>Freshness as a ranking signal.</strong> New ads get a distribution boost. Old ads get penalized. The system actively favors novelty, not just relevance.</li>
          <li><strong>Broader competition.</strong> Your ad now competes against ~100&times; more candidates for each impression. A stale ad that would have won a 1,000-candidate auction loses a 100,000-candidate one.</li>
          <li><strong>Advantage+ acceleration.</strong> Advantage+ shopping campaigns and Advantage+ creative leverage Andromeda heavily. They deliver fast results but also compress creative lifespan further.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What this means in practice</h3>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Metric</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Pre-Andromeda (2023)</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Post-Andromeda (2025&ndash;2026)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Average creative lifespan</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">4&ndash;6 weeks</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">10&ndash;14 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Time to peak CPA</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">5&ndash;7 days</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;5 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">New concepts needed/week</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;5</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">6&ndash;12+</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">CTR drop by day 10</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">10&ndash;20%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">30&ndash;50%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The practical consequence is clear: brands that relied on finding one or two winning ads per month can no longer compete. You need a continuous pipeline of fresh creative &mdash; not as a nice-to-have, but as a structural requirement of the post-Andromeda ad ecosystem. See <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">our creative testing guide</a> for the full system.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 Platform-Specific Decay Rates -->
