    <!-- 08 Extending Creative Life -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="extending">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Extending</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to extend creative life</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">You can delay fatigue, but you can&rsquo;t prevent it</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Modular variations are the primary extension tool</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Each technique adds days to weeks, not months</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">While fatigue is inevitable, there are tactics that can delay it. None of these are permanent solutions &mdash; they buy time while your pipeline produces the next batch of fresh creative.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Seven techniques to extend creative lifespan</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Swap the hook.</strong> Keep the body and CTA, replace the first 3 seconds. This is the single most effective extension tactic. The same body with a fresh hook registers as a &ldquo;new&rdquo; ad to the audience. See <a href="/hook-rate" class="text-accent hover:underline">hook rate guide</a> for hook types.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Change the thumbnail / first frame.</strong> On Meta, the thumbnail is the first thing users see in the feed. A new thumbnail can restart the creative&rsquo;s life by 5&ndash;10 days.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Re-edit with different pacing.</strong> Same footage, different cuts. Faster pacing, different music, new text overlays. Costs nothing in production but registers as fresh content to the algorithm.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Switch the creator.</strong> Same script, different face. This works because the audience&rsquo;s familiarity is visual &mdash; a new person reading the same words feels like a new ad.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Change the format.</strong> Turn a talking-head into a voiceover + B-roll. Turn a voiceover into a text-on-screen. The same message in a different wrapper extends life by 1&ndash;2 weeks.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Expand the audience.</strong> If fatigue is driven by narrow targeting, broaden your audience. A larger pool means lower frequency at the same spend level. Use Advantage+ audience on Meta for automatic expansion.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Reduce spend gradually.</strong> Instead of killing a fatiguing winner outright, reduce spend by 20&ndash;30% every 3 days. This slows frequency growth and extends the creative&rsquo;s tail, buying time for replacements.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The modular advantage</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">If your creative is built with <a href="/modular-creative" class="text-accent hover:underline">modular components</a> (interchangeable hooks, bodies, and CTAs), extending life is trivial. You simply swap one component and launch a fresh combination. A modular system with 6 hooks &times; 4 bodies &times; 3 CTAs gives you 72 unique combinations from the same production effort &mdash; weeks or months of runway before the concept is truly exhausted.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 09 The Prevention Pipeline -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="pipeline">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Pipeline</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The fatigue prevention pipeline</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">6&ndash;12 new concepts per week for active brands</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">New creative must be ready before current winners decay</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The pipeline is the product &mdash; individual ads are disposable</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The only structural solution to ad fatigue is a continuous creative pipeline. Not a burst of production followed by weeks of running the same ads. A continuous, predictable flow of new concepts, tested and iterated on a weekly cadence. The <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">creative testing system</a> is the backbone of this pipeline.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Pipeline math</h3>
        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
          <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-3">If a winning ad lasts ~10 days, and you need 3&ndash;5 active winners at any time, and your hit rate is 20&ndash;30%:</p>
          <div class="bg-bg rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-[14px] text-ink text-center mb-3">
            Winners needed &divide; Hit rate = Concepts to test<br/>
            5 &divide; 0.25 = <strong>20 concepts per testing cycle</strong>
          </div>
          <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65]">With a 10-day cycle, that means producing and testing ~20 concepts every 10 days, or roughly <strong>14 per week</strong>. This is why high-performing ad accounts need a production machine, not a one-off shoot.</p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The weekly pipeline rhythm</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Monday: Data review.</strong> Tag every running creative: Scale, Extend, Kill. Identify fatiguing winners that need iterations. Calculate remaining runway for active winners.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Tuesday: Concept &amp; script.</strong> Write new concepts based on learnings from killed and fatiguing ads. Assign to creators. Prioritize iterations of proven angles and fresh concepts (60/30/10 split).</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Wednesday&ndash;Thursday: Production.</strong> Creators shoot. Editors cut. Variations assembled. <a href="/canvas-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">UGC content</a> and AI-enhanced footage produced in parallel.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Friday: QA &amp; launch.</strong> Review all new creatives. Launch fresh batch. Begin next test cycle.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Weekend: Data collection.</strong> New ads run for 48&ndash;72 hours. Early signals begin appearing. Monday review starts the cycle again.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Pipeline by spend level</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Monthly ad spend</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">New concepts/week</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Active creatives needed</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Replacement cycle</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">$10K&ndash;$50K</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;6</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">2&ndash;3</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Every 2&ndash;3 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">$50K&ndash;$200K</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">6&ndash;12</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;5</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Weekly</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">$200K+</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">12&ndash;20+</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">5&ndash;10+</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Continuous (multiple per week)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10 Fatigue Monitoring System -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="monitoring">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">10 &mdash; Monitoring</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Building a fatigue monitoring system</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Daily monitoring of frequency, CTR, and CPA per creative</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Automated alerts when frequency hits 2.0 or CTR drops 3 days in a row</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Creative health dashboard: Green / Yellow / Red status per ad</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Reactive fatigue management &mdash; noticing CPA is up in the weekly review &mdash; is too slow. By the time weekly data shows a problem, you&rsquo;ve already wasted days of budget on a dying creative. A proper monitoring system catches fatigue at the first signal and triggers action immediately.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The creative health dashboard</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Status</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Criteria</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Action</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold" style="color: #2e7d32">Green</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Frequency &lt;2.0, CPA at/below target, CTR stable or rising</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Scale. Maintain or increase budget.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold" style="color: #f57f17">Yellow</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Frequency 2.0&ndash;2.5, CTR declining 2+ days, CPA rising &lt;20%</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Prepare replacement. Launch variations. Don&rsquo;t increase spend.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink font-semibold" style="color: #c62828">Red</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Frequency &gt;2.5, CTR dropping 3+ days, CPA &gt;20% above peak</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Reduce spend immediately. Replace. Move budget to fresh creative.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Metrics to track daily per creative</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Frequency</strong> &mdash; average times each user has seen the ad. Threshold: 2.0 (yellow), 2.5 (red).</li>
          <li><strong>CTR (click-through rate)</strong> &mdash; track the daily trend, not the absolute number. 3 consecutive days of decline = fatigue signal.</li>
          <li><strong>CPA</strong> &mdash; compare to the creative&rsquo;s own peak, not to the account average. A 30% increase from peak = action required.</li>
          <li><strong>Hook rate (3s)</strong> &mdash; declining hook rate confirms fatigue. The audience recognizes and skips the creative instantly.</li>
          <li><strong>Impression share</strong> &mdash; if the algorithm is reducing delivery, the ad is losing competitiveness.</li>
          <li><strong>Days active</strong> &mdash; simple but effective. Any creative running past 14 days on Meta should be watched closely.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Automation</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Set up automated rules in your ad platform: if frequency &gt; 2.5 AND CTR drops &gt;20% from 7-day average, automatically reduce budget by 30% and send an alert. This prevents the worst case: a dying creative burning through budget over a weekend when nobody&rsquo;s monitoring. Most ad platforms (Meta, TikTok) support rule-based automation natively.</p>
      </div>
