    <!-- 12 FAQ -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="faq">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">12 &mdash; FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "What is ad fatigue?", a: "Ad fatigue is the decline in ad performance caused by audience overexposure. When users see the same ad too many times, they stop engaging. The ad platform's algorithm detects this declining engagement and reduces the ad's delivery priority, creating a death spiral of fewer impressions, worse results, and higher CPA." },
          { q: "How do I know if my ad is fatiguing or just bad?", a: "Check the performance curve. A fatigued ad performed well initially and then declined — good CPA that rose over time, high frequency (2.5+), CTR that was strong but is now dropping. A bad ad underperforms from day one — poor CPA from launch, low frequency (the ad hasn't been shown enough to fatigue), consistently low CTR. Fatigued concepts should be iterated; bad concepts should be killed." },
          { q: "How long do ads last on Meta in 2026?", a: "Average creative lifespan on Meta is roughly 10-14 days for a scaled winning ad. Meta's Andromeda system (launched 2024) compressed lifespan significantly — down from 4-6 weeks in 2023. Higher daily spend accelerates fatigue further. Ads running at $1,000/day fatigue faster than those at $100/day." },
          { q: "What is the frequency threshold for fatigue?", a: "On Meta, fatigue typically begins when frequency hits 2.5-3.0. On TikTok, it can start as low as 1.5-2.0 because users expect more content novelty. On YouTube, the threshold is higher (3.0-4.0) because intent-based viewing means users are more tolerant of repeated ads." },
          { q: "What is the fastest way to fix a fatiguing ad?", a: "Swap the hook — replace the first 3 seconds while keeping the body and CTA intact. This is the single most effective extension technique because the opening is what the audience recognizes most strongly. A new hook on a proven body often performs like a fresh ad for another 7-14 days." },
          { q: "How many new creatives do I need per week?", a: "Depends on your ad spend. At $10K-50K/month: 3-6 new concepts per week. At $50K-200K/month: 6-12. At $200K+: 12-20 or more. The math is driven by your hit rate (typically 20-30%) and creative lifespan (~10 days). You need enough new concepts to maintain 3-5 active winners at any time." },
          { q: "What is Meta's Andromeda system and why does it matter?", a: "Andromeda is Meta's ad-ranking system, rolled out in 2024. It evaluates roughly 100,000 ad candidates per impression (up from ~1,000) and uses creative freshness as a significant ranking signal. This means new ads get a distribution boost while older ads get penalized — compressing the average creative lifespan from ~6 weeks to ~10 days." },
          { q: "Can I prevent ad fatigue entirely?", a: "No. Fatigue is inherent to paid advertising — any ad shown repeatedly to the same audience will eventually lose effectiveness. What you can do is delay fatigue (through hook swaps, audience expansion, modular variations) and outpace it (through a continuous creative pipeline). The goal is to always have fresh winners entering the rotation before current ones decay." },
          { q: "What is a creative pipeline?", a: "A creative pipeline is a continuous production system that delivers new ad concepts on a predictable weekly cadence. It includes research, scripting, production (with UGC creators, B-roll, and AI), testing, and iteration. The pipeline replaces the traditional model of periodic 'creative shoots' with an always-on creative operation." },
          { q: "Can OKAD help with ad fatigue prevention?", a: "Yes. We build and run continuous creative pipelines — strategy, scripts, UGC production, testing, and data-driven iteration on a weekly cadence. Our clients get a steady flow of fresh, tested creative instead of a handful of ads that die in two weeks. Write to us at olga@okad.agency or book a call to discuss your current fatigue challenges." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="faq-item border-b border-border">
            <div class="faq-q flex justify-between items-center gap-4 py-5 cursor-pointer">
              <span class="font-display font-semibold text-[16px] text-ink">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[20px] text-accent shrink-0 faq-icon">+</span>
            </div>
